  "body": "<p>The opening announces itself with music. Scribonia enters despite his unstable condition, determined not to let reality unravel. Aravil distrusts the invitation from the start. Ryvyt gathers his things and follows, while Pin brings his shadow companion. Beyond the threshold, a masked company is waiting aboard a vessel called the Eversong.</p><h2 id=\"the-invitation\">Every guest is smiling</h2><p>The host offers beauty, music and relief from the troubles outside. Masks fit the newcomers with unsettling precision. The deck’s guests laugh and dance, but every face turns toward the arrivals with the same smile. Looking over the railing reveals a black sea without waves.</p><p>Aravil keeps her guard. She holds the offered mask rather than putting it on, aware of being observed even while she is difficult to see. Pin accepts a mask and a little of the hospitality, sending his companion to watch. The narrator makes clear that the guests have seen where it moved; an attempted precaution has not gone unnoticed.</p><p>Scribonia warns the host that he intends to close the rift. He offers to take part only if the gathering stays peaceful, with violence promised if it turns against them. The host asks them to wait for the guest of honor. Their only stated obligation is to greet her when she arrives.</p><h2 id=\"the-dance\">Saturnia’s image on the floor</h2><p>Ryvyt admits he has never danced. Pin is more willing, though his watch continues. Scribonia drinks, takes to the floor and summons a larger visage of Saturnia to join him. For a moment he gives himself to a dance suited to the two of them.</p><p>The guests continue moving even when the music pauses. Then all the instruments fall silent at once. The dancers freeze and kneel as a woman enters. The host addresses her as Majesty.</p><p>She asks whether the travelers have ever wanted something badly enough to give anything for it, then answers for them before they can speak. Her fingers unfold with too many joints. The masked guests flicker into drowned corpses and back again. When her jaw opens impossibly wide, a chorus of sirens pours out. The invitation has become an attack.</p><h2 id=\"rebellious-shadows\">An enemy under their own feet</h2><p>The travelers’ shadows become hostile. Even Pin’s companion is caught in the change. Scribonia tries to command his own back into obedience; it moves between him and Ryvyt instead. Pin threatens darkness, and Scribonia challenges whether that will help against a shadow.</p><p>Scribonia takes a gargantuan draconic form, Brass Wrath, and prepares to breathe fire. The response is immediate: a few words from one of the leaders bring a freezing attack against the new form. Some creatures become invisible. The company’s ability to see the fight begins to divide.</p><p>Aravil chooses targets on the upper deck and fires repeated volleys before moving near Ryvyt for support. Pin asks for light and offers to move if it will help the others strike. The close, smiling gathering has become a battlefield in which even familiar outlines are unreliable.</p><h2 id=\"fighting-by-sound\">Arrows into the unseen</h2><p>Scribonia breaks free of the ice, flies toward the leading foe and attacks with claws and jaws. The host’s mask cracks as the figure falls, accusing the travelers of being bad guests. Scribonia answers that the host broke the safety owed to guests. The quarrel over hospitality continues inside the violence.</p><p>Aravil loses her sight but keeps fighting. She listens for bodies and uses her bow to test where enemies stand. When she hears her arrows connect, she asks anyone who can see to direct her toward worthwhile targets. Pin also works through failing vision, using remembered positions and the perception available to him in the ether.</p><p>The woman gives her name as Estella and continues to offer a dance. Shadowed claws strike from the travelers’ own darkness. More creatures are conjured. Her playful manner does not soften the attacks, and Scribonia’s repeated boasts do not make his companions able to see. Eventually the narrator marks him as the only one who still can.</p><h2 id=\"the-last-dance\">The dragon falls; the caster remains</h2><p>Estella’s blows finally end the draconic form, and she strikes at Scribonia himself. Pin offers her the possibility of surrender if the plan is abandoned. Scribonia refuses that mercy. With his staff, he sends a burst of arcane lightning through her and brings her down.</p><p>A remaining siren discards her sword and asks whether she can leave now that the ball has ended. The following exchange records her fall rather than a negotiated departure. The company has broken the gathering’s attack, but the account does not supply a larger history for Estella, the drowned guests or the vessel’s black sea.</p><p>Pin asks about the others’ worlds and says he has been exploring Gael’s Ember areas. The ordinary desire to exchange news returns while enemies are still being dealt with. No completed conversation or shared destination is supplied before the scene moves toward closure.</p><h2 id=\"a-contracting-opening\">Sight returns as the rift shrinks</h2><p>The rift begins to contract. Scribonia starts sealing it as his anger cools. Aravil fires on the final enemies she can locate and tries to gather components while her vision still fails her.</p><p>Her sight returns during the attempt, in time for her to see how poorly it has gone. The narrator establishes the recovery of her vision and the shrinking breach. A final successful harvest, a fully completed seal and every traveler’s return are not separately shown.</p><p>The Eversong’s promise was that the travelers could leave their troubles outside until morning. The celebration instead turned their own shadows against them. They end it through a draconic assault, spells and arrows fired toward sounds in the dark, with Aravil able to see again as the opening closes around the scene.</p><p class=\"chronicle-context-links\"><strong>Continue reading</strong> <a href=\"#rifts\">Rifts</a> · <a href=\"#scribonia\">Scribonia</a> · <a href=\"#aravil\">Aravil</a> · <a href=\"#ryvyt\">Ryvyt</a> · <a href=\"#pelegia\">Pelegia / Pin</a> · <a href=\"#saturnia\">Saturnia</a></p>",
